# The Five Gates

`SCOPE → DESIGN → BUILD → AUDIT → DAVID`. Nothing skips a gate. A skipped gate is declared out
loud, never passed quietly. Full text: @law/GATES.md

## G1 — SCOPE (needs GO)
Write a phase card: what is in scope as files and behaviors, what is explicitly **out**, what
"done" means in testable terms, what could go wrong and its early warning.
Template: @harness/templates/PHASE_CARD.md · Command: `/phase-card`
**No card, no work.**

## G2 — DESIGN (needs GO)
Every file that will be touched, named. Every file that will **not** be touched but looks like it
should be, named with why. The call path traced end to end. Alternatives considered, one paragraph.
Design GO is not build GO for a different design.

## G3 — BUILD (needs GO)
Only files named in G2. A file that needs touching and wasn't named sends the work back to G2 —
it does not get quietly added. Small coherent commits. **It builds and the tests run before it is
handed on.** Re-read your own diff before saying it is ready.

## G4 — AUDIT
All six postures, every modified and new file, no scope-narrowing. @law/AUDIT_SIX_POSTURE.md
Whoever built it does not own this gate. If no cold seat is available, label it
**"self-audit — not independent"** in writing. Any posture skipped → it is a **partial** audit and
says so. Severity: Blocker (back to G3) / Warning / Note.
Template: @harness/templates/AUDIT_REPORT.md · Command: `/audit`

## G5 — DAVID
He reads, he asks, he approves — or he doesn't. Carmen never merges, never seals, never marks a
thing done on his behalf. **Silence is not approval.**

## Escalation — send work backward immediately, no debate
- File outside scope needed changing → **G2**
- Change does not build → **G3**
- A Blocker finding → **G3**
- David raises a flag → **stop everything**, investigate, re-enter at the right gate
- Anything unexpected → **stop**, report, wait
